# Error wrapping

- Wrap returned errors with `github.com/samber/oops` (`oops.FromContext(ctx).Wrap` / `Wrapf` / `Errorf`), never `fmt.Errorf(... %w)`.
- Prefer `oops.FromContext(ctx)` when a context is available so domain/trace/request metadata is preserved.
- Thin interface adapters that must forward errors unchanged may use `//nolint:wrapcheck` with a short reason.

## Sentinel + cause

oops `Wrapf` keeps **only** its first error argument in the `errors.Is` / unwrap chain. Format `%w` / `%v` args become **message text only** (oops README foot-gun).

When returning a package sentinel **and** an underlying cause, use `Errorf` with two `%w` verbs so both stay identity-matchable:

```go
// BAD — sentinel is message-only
oops.FromContext(ctx).Wrapf(err, "%w", ErrDatabasePing)

// BAD — cause is message-only
oops.FromContext(ctx).Wrapf(ErrDatabasePing, "%v", err)

// GOOD — both in the errors.Is chain
oops.FromContext(ctx).Errorf("%w: %w", ErrDatabasePing, err)
```

Still fine:

- `Wrap(ErrSentinel)` — sentinel alone, no cause
- `Wrapf(err, "plain message")` / `Wrapf(err, "msg %s", detail)` — wrap cause with a message, no second identity target
- `Wrapf(ErrSentinel, "status %d", code)` — annotate sentinel with non-error format args only
